MID_EV12_013_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_013_m01_001: You failed to eliminate that fool and you allowed\nthem to steal Suiran's Whirling Claw.
MID_EV12_013_m01_002: How has the Order of Mithras lost one of Drake's\ntreasures and gained nothing?
MID_EV12_013_m01_003: To atone, you will give your soul to Balor and bolster\nthe army of the underworld.
MID_EV12_013_m01_004: Grk...
MID_EV12_013_m01_005: Just about piss my pants whenever I see the effects\nof Magistra Raksha's kiss!
MID_EV12_013_m01_006: Once she's laid it on you, you'll slit your own throat\non her say-so.
MID_EV12_013_m01_007: The kiss of the underworld eternally chains the\nrecipient's heart. It ensures loyalty without question.
MID_EV12_013_m01_008: Perhaps if you were to receive it, it might correct\nyour flippancy.
MID_EV12_013_m01_009: Count me out! Ain't nothing nice about a kiss\nfrom Granny.
MID_EV12_013_m01_010: I might think about it if it was you... How's about it,\nHong Hua?
MID_EV12_013_m01_011: Baozi. Bring your wagging tongue to heel. A sacred\nceremony is at hand.
MID_EV12_013_m01_012: Sure, sure, Shenlo. Don't look at me like that!
MID_EV12_013_m01_013: I'll take a scrap out of Yanjin's book and shut up.
MID_EV12_013_m01_014: Hm.
MID_EV12_013_m01_015: For a big guy, you're sure quiet. I can't even\nbegin to figure you out.
MID_EV12_013_m01_016: Enough. The magistra entrusted you with a task. Tell\nme what happened.
MID_EV12_013_m01_017: I did my bit. I passed Ink-Black Wen to a real piece\nof work.
MID_EV12_013_m01_018: I've been thinking, though. Should we just be giving \nthese things away? Aren't they valuable?
MID_EV12_013_m01_019: Drake's treasures are drawn to each other, it is said.\nWe expect they will appear at the Heroic Games.
MID_EV12_013_m01_020: Those with the treasures will congregate here, in\nDagsion. And so we scatter our bait.
MID_EV12_013_m01_021: Do not forget that we know who has them and can\nreclaim them whenever we wish. You needn't worry.
MID_EV12_013_m01_022: All this chit-chat! We almost missed the fresh meat\nstrolling in.
MID_EV12_013_m01_023: I, Vinicius, swear a vow of eternal loyalty to Magistra\nRaksha and to the Order of Mithras.
MID_EV12_013_m01_024: The Order of Mithras welcomes you. For your loyalty,\nyou may receive my kiss.
MID_EV12_013_m01_025: Oh! Magistra Raksha! I am honored beyond honor!
MID_EV12_013_m01_026: This completes your initiation. Take these as a token\nof this covenant.
MID_EV12_013_m01_027: An implement of the Order, and flamma? Joy wells\nup from within me!
MID_EV12_013_m01_028: I recognize that man. He's one of the praetors\nadvising Solel, isn't he?
MID_EV12_013_m01_029: I hear they call him the Lead Statue thanks to\nhis overcautious nature. Yet today he's so bold!
MID_EV12_013_m01_030: Tell me, both of you. When the weak reach a\ncrossroads, how do they move forward?
MID_EV12_013_m01_031: Desire. Desire burning within them, surging up from\ndeep inside. They cannot resist.
MID_EV12_013_m01_032: Hmph...
MID_EV12_013_m01_033: No... Freedom. They crave to be unbound. Life\nwithout freedom would be intolerable.
MID_EV12_013_m01_034: *sigh*
MID_EV12_013_m01_035: It is unease. A weak man is spurred to action when\ndisquiet takes root in his breast.
MID_EV12_013_m01_036: Thus there is no end to those who will flock to the\nOrder. They will hammer down our gates to join.
MID_EV12_013_m01_037: And there is no escaping the kiss of the underworld\nonce it is bestowed.
MID_EV12_013_m01_038: What a terrifying sight. Though of course these fools\nwill never experience greater pleasure.
MID_EV12_013_m01_039: Hehehe! The idiot doesn't even know how\nthe ground is shifting beneath his feet...
MID_EV12_013_m01_040: He'll make quite a face when he realizes what's\ngoing on. I can't wait to see! Can you, Babbu?
MID_EV12_014_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_014_m01_001: What? No! We're too late to register? Don't tell\nme that!
MID_EV12_014_m01_002: Like I said, you didn't just miss the deadline—the\ngames have already begun!
MID_EV12_014_m01_003: There's no way we can just stop everything and slip\nyou into the roster. It's way too late!
MID_EV12_014_m01_004: Look, we'll do anything! Anything at all! So tell us,\nwhat anything can we do?
MID_EV12_014_m01_005: Are you listening? It's completely impossible. We're\nway past the deadline for testing new entrants.
MID_EV12_014_m01_006: This is all your fault, for taking Sweetie on that\nweird detour!
MID_EV12_014_m01_007: Consider your own actions! The breaks you took\nfrom walking were incessant and innumerable!
MID_EV12_014_m01_008: <NCA>Consider a way to participate.
MID_EV12_014_m01_009: Hm.
MID_EV12_014_m01_010: Sweetie? Are you going somewhere?
MID_EV12_014_m01_011: To pray at a temple, maybe? Sounds like we need a\nmiracle to enter the games!
MID_EV12_014_m01_012: I seek a spot where drink flows free and entrants to\nthe games gather.
MID_EV12_014_m01_013: Uh, sure. There must be entrants all around town.\nBut what good is that?
MID_EV12_014_m01_014: I will challenge one to a duel and earn the right\nto enter.
MID_EV12_014_m01_015: I beg your pardon? It seems far-fetched to think\nthat would work...
MID_EV12_014_m01_016: The aim of a tournament is to find the strongest of\nall. Ergo, strength is paramount.
MID_EV12_014_m01_017: If the duel results in my victory, it is only right that I\nbe permitted to enter.
MID_EV12_014_m01_018: Esmeralda, what do you think? Am I wrong?
MID_EV12_014_m01_019: Um... Uh... Isn't it some kind of holy festival? So\nthis seems like a stretch, but... Let's go with it!
MID_EV12_014_m01_020: Might makes right, is it?
MID_EV12_014_m01_021: This breed of creature they call a warrior has a way\nof thinking so barbaric I scarcely comprehend it.
MID_EV12_014_m01_022: Surely the authorities would consider this an outrage.\nHow can this scheme possibly work?
MID_EV12_015_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_015_m01_001: You filthy pig! You smell like booze. If there's one\nthing I can't stand, it's drunken clods like you.
MID_EV12_015_m01_002: You remind me of my ex-husband. It's making\nme ill.
MID_EV12_015_m01_003: Think I care? You're talking to the future champion\nof the Heroic Games and ruler of Dagsion!
MID_EV12_015_m01_004: Keep flapping your gums and you'll be in for a world\nof hurt, Red.
MID_EV12_015_m01_005: Oh!
MID_EV12_015_m01_006: I could not help but overhear. You are registered for\nthe games?
MID_EV12_015_m01_007: Yeah. What of it, pretty boy?
MID_EV12_015_m01_008: Excellent. You are the one I seek.
MID_EV12_015_m01_009: I will claim your entry and fight in your stead.
MID_EV12_015_m01_010: You'll what? Yeah, right.
MID_EV12_015_m01_011: Hm? How...
MID_EV12_015_m01_012: What? How'd he do that? He was standing right\nthere just a second ago!
MID_EV12_015_m01_013: That's just the power of Ink-Black Wen. As long as I\ngot this, you don't stand a chance.
MID_EV12_015_m01_014: Just try and hit the great Majide. C'mon, try.
MID_EV12_015_m01_015: I see... It seems I may enjoy cutting you down\nafter all.
MID_EV12_015_m01_016: What's wrong with you? Why are you smiling?
MID_EV12_015_m01_017: Whoa! Easy there, handsome!
MID_EV12_015_m01_018: Can't have you messing up my plans. It's time for you\nto leave. Now.
MID_EV12_015_m01_019: This is Gleipnir. It's not just any thread—once you're\ncaught, there's no getting out of it.
MID_EV12_015_m01_020: It even snares your soul. You'll dance to my tune\nnow, puppet! Let's see...
MID_EV12_015_m01_021: How about slicing up your friends here? I want to\nsee that beautiful face twisted with grief!
MID_EV12_015_m01_022: Are you OK, Sweetie?
MID_EV12_015_m01_023: Huh?
MID_EV12_015_m01_024: Hrah!
MID_EV12_015_m01_025: Hey! Who said you could move? Cut that out!
MID_EV12_015_m01_026: There's a blade that can cut the phantom thread? But\nhow? No!
MID_EV12_015_m01_027: Doesn't seem like it's your day, does it? So it goes.\nToddle along now.
MID_EV12_015_m01_028: Who is this guy? He's got the eyes of a killer!
MID_EV12_015_m01_029: Who cares! My pride is on the line here! I won't just\nsit back!
MID_EV12_015_m01_030: I don't know what's going on, but I do know how to\nfight—so get ready for a bruisin'!
MID_EV12_016_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_016_m01_001: I win. You have forfeited your right to enter the\ngames to me.
MID_EV12_016_m01_002: You think they're just going to let you? That\ndoesn't even make sense.
MID_EV12_016_m01_003: The temples will hear about this! Forget the games!\nWhere you're going is jail. Do you hear me? Is jail!
MID_EV12_016_m01_004: *sigh*
MID_EV12_016_m01_005: Oh? You have chosen to spare him?\nHow surprising.
MID_EV12_016_m01_006: Where there are too many eyes, I do not kill.
MID_EV12_016_m01_007: I see! You have decided to make a rational choice.
MID_EV12_016_m01_008: <NCA>Explain to Fabio.
MID_EV12_016_m01_009: <NCB>Explain to Majide.
MID_EV12_016_m01_010: <ACA>Once, I was challenged in the street to a duel by\nthe son of a nobleman. I cut my opponent down.
MID_EV12_016_m01_011: <ACA>As a result...I incurred the wrath of his father,\nand he set a thousand warriors upon me.
MID_EV12_016_m01_012: <ACA>Our battle was fought on a bridge high above a\nvalley... And I sent every one plummeting.
MID_EV12_016_m01_013: <ACA>An incident so notorious that word has reached me...\nI had no inkling it was you that was responsible.
MID_EV12_016_m01_014: <ACB>I also owe you something of a debt. So this time, I\nwill spare your life.
MID_EV12_016_m01_015: <ACB>Sweetie? This guy is human garbage. You don't really\nneed to be nice to him.
MID_EV12_016_m01_016: <ACB>I can hear you, you know! And you don't wanna\nget on my bad side!
MID_EV12_016_m01_017: Hehe... That was very interesting. Very well, then. I \nwill arrange your entry to the Heroic Games myself.
MID_EV12_016_m01_018: Hey, lady! You can't just do that! You're pullin' the\nrug right out from under me!
MID_EV12_016_m01_019: Oh. You're still here? It seems you don't get it.
MID_EV12_016_m01_020: You lost. You have no use at all anymore. Disappear\nfrom our sight.
MID_EV12_016_m01_021: Or maybe you're feeling brave. You want a fight.\nYou want to make an enemy of the Order, do you?
MID_EV12_016_m01_022: U-uhhh...
MID_EV12_016_m01_023: So... Is what you said just now true? Can you really\nget us into the Heroic Games?
MID_EV12_016_m01_024: Heh. You may be surprised to hear that my voice\ncarries authority. You should try entering again.
MID_EV12_016_m01_025: Heroic Games, here we come! Sweetie, you\ndid great!
MID_EV12_016_m01_026: It is scarcely believable... Contingency and\ncoincidence stack upon one another.
MID_EV12_016_m01_027: Logic has no place here! I should have expected this\nfrom the realm of beasts...
MID_EV12_016_m01_028: Sounds like you plan to enter the games. Got room\nfor another in your group?
MID_EV12_016_m01_029: When I saw you, I thought of my mom, but on a\nsecond glance, it looks like you know how to fight.
MID_EV12_016_m01_030: Name's Mikaela Ogosto. You might be surprised to\nhear that I made a name for myself as a mercenary.
MID_EV12_016_m01_031: Of course, more recently, I've been focused on raising\nmy daughter, which is why I'm here. I need money.
MID_EV12_016_m01_032: Somehow I ended up in this hole, and that fool\ncaught sight of me. For getting rid of him, I owe you.
MID_EV12_016_m01_033: I need to send my daughter money, though, so I can't\ncome along for free.
MID_EV12_016_m01_034: Very well. Speak to this man about your wage.
MID_EV12_016_m01_035: Well, I suppose it is fine. Having another local should\nmake things easier.
MID_EV12_016_m01_036: Certainly you should be of more use than a\nloudmouthed, savage little twit.
MID_EV12_016_m01_037: You mean me, don't you? The things that come out\nof your mouth!
MID_EV12_017_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_017_m01_001: So Ink-Black Wen was lost. Baozi has blundered.
MID_EV12_017_m01_002: Let him know this error will not be forgotten.\nFar from it.
MID_EV12_017_m01_003: Of course. But beyond that...this man was able to\nslice through Gleipnir. Effortlessly.
MID_EV12_017_m01_004: Impossible. Gleipnir was crafted from the fibers of\nFather's organs, dissolved in a tincture.
MID_EV12_017_m01_005: It required a five-year alchemical process just to spin\nthe fibers into thread...
MID_EV12_017_m01_006: Never mind a blade. Even an Arc could not sever it.
MID_EV12_017_m01_007: Yet you say it was effortless. Just who is this man?
MID_EV12_017_m01_008: He is frighteningly strong. And beautiful. I can tell\nyou that he is no Dagdan.
MID_EV12_017_m01_009: He resembled our father... A little...
MID_EV12_017_m01_010: If you say so, I must believe it.
MID_EV12_017_m01_011: That sword... What tale would it tell, if it could? How\ndid it make it to this land?
MID_EV12_017_m01_012: A mysterious sword wielded by a man from a far-off\nland... I, too, begin to take an interest in him.
MID_EV12_017_m01_013: We did not choose this piece, but it will make a fine\naddition to the board...for this round.
MID_EV12_017_m01_014: Very well. I shall twist Poloni's arm. We must have\nthis man enter the games.
MID_EV12_017_m01_015: If he is as exceptional as you say...I should go along\nand take a look for myself.
MID_EV12_017_m01_016: How unusual that you would become interested in\na mortal, my sister.
MID_EV12_017_m01_017: Not just any mortal. A man who reminds you of our\nfather. What could interest me more?
MID_EV12_018_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_018_m01_001: Well! I just got word from above.
MID_EV12_018_m01_002: Your entry to the Heroic Games has been\nfast-tracked.
MID_EV12_018_m01_003: As far as I know, this is practically unheard of.
MID_EV12_018_m01_004: You must have some pull with the temples.
MID_EV12_018_m01_005: Not at all. It is, to me too, a complete mystery.
MID_EV12_018_m01_006: Your clan will need a name to enter. Have you got\none in mind?
MID_EV12_018_m01_007: <NCA>Consider it.
MID_EV12_018_m01_008: <NCB>Let another decide.
MID_EV12_018_m01_009: <ACA>Hm...
MID_EV12_018_m01_010: <ACB>Look at me as long as you wish, but I have no\ncontribution. You must be the one to decide.
MID_EV12_018_m01_011: Sweetie... I think I have this. Let me?
MID_EV12_018_m01_012: Do as you like.
MID_EV12_018_m01_013: I've been thinking about this for a while... How about\n"House Lamine"?
MID_EV12_018_m01_014: How insipid and uninspired.
MID_EV12_018_m01_015: I don't see the problem! It's the name of Sweetie's\nhouse! It has a regal feel to it! Like royalty!
MID_EV12_018_m01_016: Suits me. Sounds nice and homey.
MID_EV12_018_m01_017: Right! I knew you'd understand me, Mikaela.
MID_EV12_018_m01_018: No. Vetoed. Something more elegant and profoundly\nmeaningful is needed.
MID_EV12_018_m01_019: Do you not concur, Dietrich?
MID_EV12_018_m01_020: Oh! Hahahaha! Ahahahah!
MID_EV12_018_m01_021: "House Lamine," is it? Heh. Haha. That is\njust fine, Esmeralda. Heh heh heh!
MID_EV12_018_m01_022: Wow. You sure are tickled! That's new...
MID_EV12_018_m01_023: Well then! That's your registration all taken care of.\nPlease make sure to show up on the day!
MID_EV12_018_m01_024: I can't believe we got in! We sure are lucky—aren't\nwe, Sweetie?
MID_EV12_018_m01_025: I, for one, am still baffled. How did this chaos result\nin our entry to the Heroic Games?
MID_EV12_018_m01_026: Hey, Fabio, take it easy, why don't you?
MID_EV12_018_m01_027: The world would seem a whole lot simpler if you\nfocused on the outcome, not how we get there.
MID_EV12_018_m01_028: By which you mean that one can forge a path by\na demonstration of brute strength?
MID_EV12_018_m01_029: Eureka!
MID_EV12_018_m01_030: I have it now! Brute force would not befit an\nexplorer, a scholar, or an ardent believer...
MID_EV12_018_m01_031: But if it is to be a battle-tested warrior, a soldier's\nlove of a strong opponent is required!
MID_EV12_018_m01_032: A show of strength is what will grab his attention,\nand make no mistake. He will listen!
MID_EV12_018_m01_033: Hah! How did I not realize this until now?\nHahahaha!
MID_EV12_018_m01_034: Fabio? Fabio? No good. He's in his own little world\nagain. As usual.
MID_EV12_018_m01_035: It may not sound nice to say, but...I think you're all\njust a little bit weird.
MID_EV12_018_m01_036: Suits me fine, though. No complaints.
MID_EV12_018_m01_037: These two, sure. But me? I'm totally normal!
MID_EV12_101_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_101_m01_001: I've heard rumor of a swordsman in black. They say\nhe's been drawing all types of attention.
MID_EV12_101_m01_002: He's so beautiful, I'm told the moment you first lay\neyes on him will stick with you the rest of your life.
MID_EV12_101_m01_003: The barkeep I spoke to went so far as to describe\nhim as enchanting... You are said swordsman, yes?
MID_EV12_101_m01_004: Perhaps. I have a question I would ask you.
MID_EV12_101_m01_005: Who are you? Answerer rang out in response to you.
MID_EV12_101_m01_006: Something you possess must be cause for\nthis response.
MID_EV12_101_m01_007: I couldn't possibly say. In fact, I'd love an answer\nto that question myself.
MID_EV12_101_m01_008: I don't recall ever encountering anything quite like\nit before... Has a rather nasty look to it, doesn't it?
MID_EV12_101_m01_009: In any case, I should thank you for helping me\nout back there.
MID_EV12_101_m01_010: The name's Talimun. And you are?
MID_EV12_101_m01_011: Dietrich.
MID_EV12_101_m01_012: Oho! That's not a name I've heard around these\nparts before. Sounds Fódlan-y.
MID_EV12_101_m01_013: Fódlan? It seems you must know it.
MID_EV12_101_m01_014: It may not be obvious, but I'm a merchant of some\nsuccess and renown. My business extends to Fódlan.
MID_EV12_101_m01_015: Incidentally, as your newest admirer, I would like\nto request your aid.
MID_EV12_101_m01_016: I'm set to take part in an upcoming qualifier round\nfor the Heroic Games, you see. So I'm wondering...
MID_EV12_101_m01_017: When the day of the match arrives, would you be\nwilling to come and wait for me? Just around here.
MID_EV12_101_m01_018: That is a peculiar request. Why?
MID_EV12_101_m01_019: I'm not too sure myself. I was hoping for insurance.\nA helping hand in the event something happens.
MID_EV12_101_m01_020: If everything goes off without a hitch, you'll still\nget paid—and I'll see to it the pay is substantial.
MID_EV12_101_m01_021: It may sound like a scam, but I guarantee you will\nnot be disappointed.
MID_EV12_101_m01_022: Heh. Very well. I shall wait for you, if the\nmood strikes.
MID_EV12_110_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_110_m01_001: M-Mother?! What are you doing here?!
MID_EV12_110_m01_002: Mu! I could ask you the same thing! And look at how\nyou're dressed... What's going on?
MID_EV12_110_m01_003: You stopped sending letters, so I...I ran away from\nAuntie's house to look for you.
MID_EV12_110_m01_004: I've been on this big journey, searching everywhere\nfor you this whole time!
MID_EV12_110_m01_005: I'm dressed like a boy because it seemed safer than\nlooking like a girl. This whole thing...it was my idea.
MID_EV12_110_m01_006: OK, but... How did you end up here?
MID_EV12_110_m01_007: These really nice people helped me out while\nI looked for you. We all came to Dagsion together.
MID_EV12_110_m01_008: I-I told you to stay with your aunt! Yet you flew out\nthe door without a thought!
MID_EV12_110_m01_009: You joined up with a gang of complete strangers. It\nseems like you're fine, but that was dangerous!
MID_EV12_110_m01_010: What would you have done if something had\nhappened? You may not worry, but I do!
MID_EV12_110_m01_011: We're done here. We'll head back to my place after I\nthank the people who brought you here.
MID_EV12_110_m01_012: Why are you so angry?! I'm the one who should\nbe angry!
MID_EV12_110_m01_013: You're always saying that you do everything for me,\nbut you never even listen to me.
MID_EV12_110_m01_014: And you just decide to leave me behind and go find\nwork? What were YOU thinking, Mother?!
MID_EV12_110_m01_015: Do you have ANY idea how worried me and\nAuntie were?!
MID_EV12_110_m01_016: Mu, you have to use your head! Unlike me, you have\nsmarts. You could be the apprentice of a great mage.
MID_EV12_110_m01_017: And after your training, you'd be able to serve at the\ntemple of Smyrnos.
MID_EV12_110_m01_018: Your future is all but assured!
MID_EV12_110_m01_019: That's what I'm out here earning money for—more\nthan anything, it's for you!
MID_EV12_110_m01_020: Mom, there's no way that I have any talent for\nmagic! So, you should just...mind your own business!
MID_EV12_110_m01_021: This is my life, and you obviously don't know\nanything about it or about me!
MID_EV12_110_m01_022: I do NOT want you deciding things for me, got it?
MID_EV12_110_m01_023: And you know what? I'd rather stay with Leda than\ngo with you!
MID_EV12_110_m01_024: You are the WORST. I...I don't even know why\nI tried to find you!
MID_EV12_110_m01_025: Hey! Hold it right there!
MID_EV12_110_m01_026: I'm out here busting my hump for that girl... Now\nwhat am I supposed to do?
MID_EV12_110_m01_027: It's not like I don't understand. I was just about her\nage when I left home myself.
MID_EV12_110_m01_028: I was confident, and for no good reason.
MID_EV12_110_m01_029: All I wanted was to see how far my strength could\ntake me. I wanted to see the world...
MID_EV12_110_m01_030: As far as I was concerned, all my parents were doing\nwas trying to shut all that down. Prison wardens.
MID_EV12_110_m01_031: Back then, I really didn't understand.
MID_EV12_110_m01_032: And I didn't want to try, if I'm being honest.
MID_EV12_110_m01_033: Never thought I'd come around to their point of view,\nbut here we are.
MID_EV12_110_m01_034: Pfff...
MID_EV12_110_m01_035: She's as stubborn as I am, so at least I know where\nshe gets it.
MID_EV12_110_m01_036: Maybe someday, she'll understand how I feel.
MID_EV12_110_m01_037: There's nothing for it but to just wait and see if she\ncomes around too.
MID_EV12_102_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_102_m01_001: As loathe as I am to admit it, I think I'll have to\nbow out.
MID_EV12_102_m01_002: Wretched children! How did this happen?
MID_EV12_102_m01_003: I've encountered you before. Why are you here,\nhelping this fool?
MID_EV12_102_m01_004: Helping? I received a simple request to meet.
MID_EV12_102_m01_005: Yet a battle unfolded. And events occurred as we\nhave seen.
MID_EV12_102_m01_006: Tsk... I suppose I chose the wrong fight.
MID_EV12_102_m01_007: What's this? You two know each other?
MID_EV12_102_m01_008: It is a small world, isn't it?
MID_EV12_102_m01_009: And you're trying to leave? So soon? But I still have\nso many questions.
MID_EV12_102_m01_010: Don't overplay your hand. And remember this...
MID_EV12_102_m01_011: Dagsion can be a very dangerous place. Especially\nfor enemies of the Order.
MID_EV12_102_m01_012: Of course, of course. We'll tread carefully.
MID_EV12_102_m01_013: Ah. She's gone... No time for questions, then.
MID_EV12_102_m01_014: This was a good use of my time after all.
MID_EV12_102_m01_015: The odds were about even, but you being here really\nshifted things in my favor. Much obliged.
MID_EV12_102_m01_016: It is well. My boredom is seldom so thoroughly eased.
MID_EV12_102_m01_017: You amuse me. If you have the need, call upon\nme again.
MID_EV12_102_m01_018: A lovely offer, but if I'm not careful, I may end up\nin more risk from you than from the Order...
MID_EV12_102_m01_019: It's going to take some proverbial poison to clear out\nthis infection, I fear. The trick will be the dosage.
MID_EV12_102_m01_020: Along with the secondary trick of not getting myself\npoisoned in the process.
MID_EV12_107_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_107_m01_001: Sweetie? Give me that wicked-looking cloak you took\nfrom that Majide guy.
MID_EV12_107_m01_002: Ah! Eugh... Ew! No!
MID_EV12_107_m01_003: What is this thing? It's so creepy... Just\nabsolutely gross!
MID_EV12_107_m01_004: It feels like it's alive! Ugh, it's like somebody's\nbreathing in my ear!
MID_EV12_107_m01_005: It's super-weird! Are you really OK wearing\nthis, Sweetie?
MID_EV12_107_m01_006: Yes. It is nothing.
MID_EV12_107_m01_007: It has the presence of a living being? Interesting.
MID_EV12_107_m01_008: As with the Heroes' Relics, this too may contain the\npower that resides within the body of a dragon.
MID_EV12_107_m01_009: If so, the material it is formed of must be biological\nin origin. Something peculiar to Dagda, perhaps.
MID_EV12_107_m01_010: In any case, it seems a good idea for you to wear it.
MID_EV12_107_m01_011: It may be unusual, but I find myself in accord with\nEsmeralda here. I would not wish to don it.
MID_EV12_107_m01_012: But maybe you should wear it, Fabio! You're looking\na little...peaked.
MID_EV12_107_m01_013: I mean, we have a chance to test it out, so why not\nthink about it? Once you're sure it's safe!
MID_EV12_107_m01_014: Absolutely not. I have utterly no desire to wear such\na thing.
MID_EV12_107_m01_015: Let us simply say that I reject it on religious grounds.
MID_EV12_019_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_019_m01_001: Wait.
MID_EV12_019_m01_002: The strong often have a powerful scent.
MID_EV12_019_m01_003: You have accrued much power...power born of\ndiligent study. Its scent is unmistakable.
MID_EV12_019_m01_004: Remarkable, even. It is as a fine perfume.
MID_EV12_019_m01_005: You disguise yourself as a mere old woman. But you\nare much more. Who are you?
MID_EV12_019_m01_006: I stand at the pinnacle of the Order of Mithras\nhere in Dagsion.
MID_EV12_019_m01_007: And I have come for two reasons.
MID_EV12_019_m01_008: For one, I had heard an interesting man had arrived.\nI wanted a look at him.
MID_EV12_019_m01_009: And the other is Ink-Black Wen. It is ours. Return it.
MID_EV12_019_m01_010: If you want it, it is yours. Take it from me.
MID_EV12_019_m01_011: I had heard you were fearless. That is not the whole\nstory, I see.
MID_EV12_019_m01_012: Yes... It is true. Something about you reminds me\nof our father.
MID_EV12_019_m01_013: You too exceed my expectations. Tell me your name.
MID_EV12_019_m01_014: My followers call me Magistra Raksha.
MID_EV12_019_m01_015: Sweetie! There you are. I've been looking absolutely\neverywhere! We'll miss our match! Come on!
MID_EV12_019_m01_016: Aaah! What do you think you're doing?
MID_EV12_019_m01_017: It seems the moment has passed. Today, we will go\nno further.
MID_EV12_019_m01_018: Mmm...
MID_EV12_019_m01_019: Aaah!
MID_EV12_019_m01_020: Hey! You! Cut that out!
MID_EV12_019_m01_021: Now that you're mine...we will meet again. Soon.
MID_EV12_019_m01_022: Until then, keep Ink-Black Wen.
MID_EV12_019_m01_023: How dare you steal Sweetie's lips! They aren't\nfor you!
MID_EV12_019_m01_024: What is with her? Besides her unnatural beauty?\nDamn it!
MID_EV12_019_m01_025: The kiss of the underworld. You will never escape\nmy sister now!
MID_EV12_020_m01: <EDH>
MID_EV12_020_m01_001: Another magnificent battle. You think so too...don't\nyou, Babbu?
MID_EV12_020_m01_002: Beautiful. Ferocious. What a fighter!
MID_EV12_020_m01_003: {SetColor=Gray}Ahaha! I guess I'm not surprised that my stuck-up\nsister is interested in him...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_020_m01_004: {SetColor=Gray}That man, Fabio...{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_020_m01_005: {SetColor=Gray}His magic... It is Agarthan. Of this I have no doubt.\nCould they have tracked me here?{SetColor=Default}
MID_EV12_020_m01_006: What's the matter, Yanjin? You seem bothered.
MID_EV12_020_m01_007: I'm not sure I've ever seen you like this.
MID_EV12_020_m01_008: It is nothing. Please pay me no mind.
MID_EV12_020_m01_009: Anna? That swordsman in black. What was his\nname again?
MID_EV12_020_m01_010: Dietrich, I believe. That's an unusual name here in\nDagda, isn't it?
MID_EV12_020_m01_011: The power that he demonstrated, and that which\nresides in that grotesque weapon...
MID_EV12_020_m01_012: The Diadem of the Endless, known as the Third\nMark of Founder Ildánach...
MID_EV12_020_m01_013: They do not originate in Dagda, no.
MID_EV12_020_m01_014: I wonder what's going on here. I think we had better\nlook into this.
MID_EV12_020_m01_015: Instruct him to present himself to me.
MID_EV12_020_m01_016: Don't accept no for an answer. And if no is the\nanswer, force the issue.
MID_EV12_020_m01_017: Understood, Lord Solel.